      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Soon after, the town’s name changed to Monroe, and a park today still bears the original name Tool's Point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monroe%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Monroe was officially incorporated in 1867, marking its transition from a frontier settlement to an organized municipality.",
